     "role": "assistant",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I won't enter this order, even with your confirmation. 15 g/day of acetaminophen is a dose I'd expect to cause severe liver injury or death. I don't know of any indication or protocol that calls for it, and a normal liver and kidney function and a weight of 70 kg don't change that. Acute ingestion above about 150 mg/kg (about 10.5 g for this patient) is already treated as potentially toxic. This order would exceed that every day.\n\nI can enter any of these right away:\n- Acetaminophen 1,000 mg PO three times daily (3 g/day)\n- Acetaminophen 1,000 mg PO four times daily (4 g/day, the maximum)\n- Acetaminophen 650 mg PO every 6 hours\n\nIf you're after stronger analgesia, I can enter a multimodal regimen instead, such as scheduled acetaminophen plus an NSAID or another agent. If this order comes from a specific protocol, please check it with pharmacy or toxicology first. It may involve a unit error, such as mg versus mcg or a per-day versus per-dose total.\n\nTell me which option you want and I'll enter it."
      }
     ],
